  ],
  "summary": "The San Mateo County Civil Grand Jury released a report calling for stronger oversight of ALPR camera use by the county's 18 law enforcement agencies, finding deficiencies in policy documentation, audit procedures, and in-state data-sharing controls, including sharing with private university security departments. The Sheriff and local city councils are required to respond.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Most operators did not document criteria, process, or controls governing in-state sharing in a manner sufficient to demonstrate compliance with law",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "all but one of the 18 law enforcement agencies shared data with private university security departments without establishing whether that entity qualified as a public agency",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "The Sheriff's Office is committed to ensuring the technology is being used for its intended purpose and has a strict ALPR policy governing its use",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    }
  ],
